---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const oses = [
  ['Windows 10 / 11', 'ipconfig /flushdns', 'Command Prompt or PowerShell, run as Administrator is not required.'],
  ['macOS (modern)', 'sudo dscacheutil -flushcache; sudo killall -HUP mDNSResponder', 'One line, both parts. Sudo required.'],
  ['Linux (systemd)', 'sudo resolvectl flush-caches', 'Default on Ubuntu/Debian/Fedora today.'],
  ['Linux (nscd)', 'sudo service nscd restart', 'Older servers using nscd.'],
  ['Linux (dnsmasq)', 'sudo systemctl restart dnsmasq', 'Small-server default.'],
  ['Chrome (any OS)', 'chrome://net-internals/#dns → Clear host cache', 'Also clear sockets at chrome://net-internals/#sockets.'],
];

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is flush dns cache in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="How to Flush DNS Cache (Windows, macOS, Linux, Chrome)" description="Flush your DNS cache on every platform: Windows ipconfig /flushdns, macOS dscacheutil, Linux systemd-resolved, and Chrome's internal cache."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Flush DNS Cache</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Flush DNS Cache</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      Changed a DNS record and still seeing the old site? Your own computer is often the last cache to
      let go. Here is the flush command for every platform.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-3">
      {oses.map(([os, cmd, note]) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-ink">{os}</p>
          <pre class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-soft">{cmd}</pre>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">{note}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="rich-text mt-10">
      <h2>When flushing helps (and when it doesn't)</h2>
      <p>
        Flushing clears <em>your device's</em> cache. If the old record is still cached at your ISP's
        resolver or a public resolver, flushing locally won't help, that cache expires on its TTL
        schedule. Verify what resolvers currently see with the
        <a href="/dns-propagation-checker/">propagation checker</a>: if the world sees the new value and
        you don't, flush. If nobody sees it yet, wait.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is flush dns cache in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/dns-propagation/">DNS propagation explained</a></li>
        <li><a href="/site-down-after-dns-change/">Site down after a DNS change?</a></li>
      </ul>

    <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/40 px-5 py-3">
      <span class="grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-accent to-violet font-display text-xs font-bold text-canvas">PD</span>
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">PromptDNS Team</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">Last updated: August 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
